f Nightmares to give us Fomorian/Thallain Houses and some content about Horrors rising that need dealing with.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused with Dauntain, hella cool name but I'm still a bit confused on how to use them. Like one of them is a living contagion that can infect others with their offal, talk about topical.<br /> <br /> I would have liked more on the Red Star and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> I do like interesting bits they gave us in the NPC section with the Vampires and the like.<br /> <br /> Over all solid, especially the core C20 book that really shines even among the 20th ann books.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened to the Hsein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:08:32-07:00","id":1406782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> they\u2019re still around, but they\u2019re more closely related to Western Kithain in C20 than they were in Land of Eight Million Dreams.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> did I get that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:18:30-07:00","id":1406855,"title":"","content":"The Hsien rules are a bit more polished and updated. And they are pretty much Fae that aren\u2019t tied to the dreaming but instead tied to Heaven, like they even got a wyrd form. And Tanuki don\u2019t turn into badgers anymore. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T17:40:13-07:00","id":1406866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1406855#post1406855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hsien rules are a bit more polished and updated. And they are pretty much Fae that aren\u2019t tied to the dreaming but instead tied to Heaven, like they even got a wyrd form. And Tanuki don\u2019t turn into badgers anymore. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Heaven the High Umbra? Like the Nunnehi are tied to the Middle Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T18:54:38-07:00","id":1406874,"title":"","content":"The Hsien occupied that controversial place that so many Asian splats that WW put out did - interesting but with a valid concern regarding Orientalism and whether or not making them so clearly distinct from their \u2018standard\u2019 counterparts was good or necessary.<br /> <br /> For the Hsien especially, C20 does a lot to ground them into Changelings in general but provide some distinctions and unique rules for flair, twist, and context. Jade replaces Cold Iron, they use different Legacies, they have a distinct Wyld form - although it\u2019s somewhat similar to what other changelings have, they can gain energy through human religious rites and communal observance, and they practice a distinct rite from the Changeling Way. Plus Five Elemental alchemy.<br /> <br /> I like the Hsien and how they\u2019ve entered into an area where, like the Nunnehi &amp; Menehune, they\u2019ve entered an area where changelings can have cultural differences but still be recognizably the same class of entities.<br /> <br /> As far as their connection to The Heavens, it could be the High Umbra or Middle Umbra depending on your interpretation imo, but either way it connects to the Hsien\u2019s role as \u201clittle gods\u201d who are now trapped on earth, outside the Celestial Bureaucracy, until the world can be restored to its proper order - whatever that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:32:43-07:00","id":1406881,"title":"","content":"I like the C20 version of the hsien better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:47:03-07:00","id":1406885,"title":"","content":"Yeah C20 pretty much just clean up some errors, and added the police that Hsien never got because they never got a revised Edition.<br /> <br /> Because Changeling never got a Revised their C20 edition stands out even more then the other games, as even wraith got a revised era game update with Greatwar.<br /> <br /> The Land of Eightmillion Dreams is still useful for the added lore, background and rules concerning things like how their version of Reincarnation and Possession works. Its interesting their version of Nobles are more Inanimae then Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T05:11:24-07:00","id":1406950,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> what do you think of the Nyan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:42:59-07:00","id":1406966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1406950#post1406950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> what do you think of the Nyan?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are interesting, but as you mentioned its odd their name is the Japanese onomatopoeia for cat sounds, but I guess its like how Pok\u00e9mon has Mew. It opens the doors for a Frog Hirayanu called Kerokero though :P. Bakeneko would be a more fitting name. But ultimately not the biggest problem. They made them fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T08:04:25-07:00","id":1406970,"title":"","content":"Cool. I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T10:32:35-07:00","id":1406992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1406866#post1406866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Heaven the High Umbra? Like the Nunnehi are tied to the Middle Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heaven seems to be Umbral, maybe even Deep Umbra making it the other side of the coin of the Deep Dreaming. But the Wu Tian Immortals have ties to Heaven and it has connections to the Umbra and DarkUmbra (the Underworld). So Heaven/Tian may be something akin to the Antithesis of Yomi Wan (The Hell Dimension of Asia that overlaps the Umbra and Dark Umbra). At its simplest it could be a Near Umbral Realm that is guarded exceedingly well, like Malfeas. But its Probably a deeper level of Reality. Astral High Umbra has access to Heavens but they seem to be facets of Humankinds collective Psyche. The Heaven of the Hsien is probably more comparable to a Realm that you enter from the Near Umbra but that stretches into the Deep Umbra, Malfeas seems to do this as does the Aetherial Realm and I would say Flux.<br /> <br /> <br /> And when talking about a New High King in a different thread but it would totally be appropriate here. I think after Reading the Shining Host Duke Aslan returning from his Quest to Find Arcadia would make the ideal replacement for King David. He was the Ultimate Idealized Sidhe and Questing for half a century in the Dreaming would probably have retarded his Aging if he makes it back sane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:08:26-07:00","id":1407020,"title":"","content":"Changeling has always possessed an odd niche of the setting cosmology, which has always had a subjective streak to make matters even more complicated, so I\u2019m pretty open to most arguments about what could be the Heaven of the Hsien alongside what/where the Dreaming or Higher Hunting Grounds or such are.<br /> <br /> As for the High King situation, I like David but I could also see Aslan returning having worked potentially. In my opinion the main problems are word count and the question of just how far 20th edition could push the metaplot. From a purely pragmatic perspective, the return of King David and leaving it mysterious for the ST to work out is probably the most efficient in terms of word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:50:48-07:00","id":1407024,"title":"","content":"From which book is Duke Aslan and his quest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:52:36-07:00","id":1407037,"title":"","content":"\u2018Shining Host\u2019 according to Eldagusto.<br /> <br /> It was the closest thing we got to a \u2018Kithbook: Sidhe\u2019 and also served to layout a lot of how Arcadian society and nobility worked and functioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T17:18:40-07:00","id":1407052,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> I personally love all three Books of Houses (Noblesse Oblige, Pour L\u2019Amour et Liberte and Book of Lost Houses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T17:46:02-07:00","id":1407055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1407052#post1407052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I personally love all three Books of Houses (Noblesse Oblige, Pour L\u2019Amour et Liberte and Book of Lost Houses).</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m working my way through them right now starting with Noblesse oblige. Since I before I only read portions of my copies. Been on a major Changeling kick lately. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T21:41:06-07:00","id":1407075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1407055#post1407055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m working my way through them right now starting with Noblesse oblige. Since I before I only read portions of my copies. Been on a major Changeling kick lately. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!! Changeling is an awesome game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T21:46:23-07:00","id":1407077,"title":"","content":"I feel that Changeling is the gameline that is updated and revised just enough with the 20th books where the hard part is over while also having soooo much that could be expanded upon. Like Vampire and Werewolf are mostly complete. Kueijin and Demon need the most fundamental updates. But Changeling got the fundamentals out of the way while having so much left unexplored that it is perfect for the Storytellers vault. And its so easy to customize!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:28:24-07:00","id":1407113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1407077#post1407077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Changeling is the gameline that is updated and revised just enough with the 20th books where the hard part is over while also having soooo much that could be expanded upon. Like Vampire and Werewolf are mostly complete. Kueijin and Demon need the most fundamental updates. But Changeling got the fundamentals out of the way while having so much left unexplored that it is perfect for the Storytellers vault. And its so easy to customize!</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T05:59:41-07:00","id":1407910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1406782#post1406782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> they\u2019re still around, but they\u2019re more closely related to Western Kithain in C20 than they were in Land of Eight Million Dreams.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> did I get that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike that I hoped that the writers kept the Hsein but also added actual Asian Changlings, and be more diverse then Just China and Japan, while saying the Hsein are also their.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:16:48-07:00","id":1407914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1407910#post1407910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dislike that I hoped that the writers kept the Hsein but also added actual Asian Changlings, and be more diverse then Just China and Japan, while saying the Hsein are also their.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I'm happy with that because It allows me to do my own write ups. My Headcanon the Changelings in Asia are just the Fae that weren't drafted into heaven or that that went AWOL before the Hsien were exiled. So I have Changeling Variants of the Hsien splats, plus some extra ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:29:02-07:00","id":1407977,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> I agree with both you guys about Asian Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T04:09:57-07:00","id":1408330,"title":"","content":"Back in the 90s, there was a website of fan material for the various World of Darkness gamelines called B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness. One guy made a bunch of Kith submissions based on real-world beliefs about inhuman but humanoid creatures from around the world. At one point, for ease of reference, I copied all of them onto an Angelfire-hosted website. B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness has long since disappeared from the web; but the copy I made is still out there. Indeed, I couldn't take it down even if I wanted to: I've long since lost both the email address and the password that I used to set up that archive. <br /> <br /> Note that this predated the Hsien. But my own head-canon has always held that Changeling's have always had a much more diverse selection of Kiths throughout the world, including in East Asia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T04:15:26-07:00","id":1408474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408330#post1408330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the 90s, there was a website of fan material for the various World of Darkness gamelines called B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness. One guy made a bunch of Kith submissions based on real-world beliefs about inhuman but humanoid creatures from around the world. At one point, for ease of reference, I copied all of them onto an Angelfire-hosted website. B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness has long since disappeared from the web; but the copy I made is still out there. Indeed, I couldn't take it down even if I wanted to: I've long since lost both the email address and the password that I used to set up that archive.<br /> <br /> Note that this predated the Hsien. But my own head-canon has always held that Changeling's have always had a much more diverse selection of Kiths throughout the world, including in East Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>XD Okay I didn't know there was a salvaged arch floating around with all the old stuff.<br /> <br /> Well I plan to work on a project for Changelings of Asia and a Hsien Expansion based off my headcanon stuff. It might be after a general kith/art expansion, and maybe after my Elohim Gallain project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:24:44-07:00","id":1408483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408474#post1408474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XD Okay I didn't know there was a salvaged arch floating around with all the old stuff.<br /> <br /> Well I plan to work on a project for Changelings of Asia and a Hsien Expansion based off my headcanon stuff. It might be after a general kith/art expansion, and maybe after my Elohim Gallain project.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hsien expansion sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Who are the Elohim Gallain? Are they related to the Angels from DtF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T11:32:24-07:00","id":1408520,"title":"","content":"All right, make Dreaming Changlings for Asia ,that are not the Hsein, also I feel that House Balor has been way watered down, do they still want to have the Formorians to rule the world and murder all the nobles?<br /> <br /> And be super allies of the Black Spiral Dancers . Like of the three houses detailed in the second house book only Alli was playable as not a horrid monster that constantly kills people Weekly or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T11:37:16-07:00","id":1408521,"title":"","content":"I feel like House Balor as presented leans into the idea that they\u2019re hiding most of the goals of their agenda but I do agree that C20 seems to have turned down, or at least obfuscated, the darkness of their nature and how they were probably the most outright villainous of the Unseelie Houses, which is saying something with the Leanhaun around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T12:26:49-07:00","id":1408530,"title":"","content":"The Leanhaun are like the ultimate Ravagers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:44:02-07:00","id":1408570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408483#post1408483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hsien expansion sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Who are the Elohim Gallain? Are they related to the Angels from DtF?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I am working on making a Fae group based on the Abrahamic lore they are divided by the court of Lilim, Fae based on the principles of Freedom and independence exposed by Lilith and the court of Ruh, Elohim of the Holy Spirit who are trying to find out where God and the Angelic Host are and be redeemed back to full angel status. I have houses for both Courts, with the Ruh having Houses based on the First and Last Court, and the Lilim having Houses based on the Gardens of Lilith, Iadabaoth and Iblis. Their Kinain are Nephilim and Cambions but preshattering Nephilim also are a Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:46:24-07:00","id":1408571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408520#post1408520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, make Dreaming Changlings for Asia ,that are not the Hsein, also I feel that House Balor has been way watered down, do they still want to have the Formorians to rule the world and murder all the nobles?<br /> <br /> And be super allies of the Black Spiral Dancers . Like of the three houses detailed in the second house book only Alli was playable as not a horrid monster that constantly kills people Weekly or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah being kin to Blackspirals by oath and Blood would be a major Redflag for anyone you would think!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:19:24-07:00","id":1408597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408521#post1408521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like House Balor as presented leans into the idea that they\u2019re hiding most of the goals of their agenda but I do agree that C20 seems to have turned down, or at least obfuscated, the darkness of their nature and how they were probably the most outright villainous of the Unseelie Houses, which is saying something with the Leanhaun around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Leanhaun Have to weekly ruin someone\u2019s life just to not die, and what self respecting GM would let someone play a Balor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:45:57-07:00","id":1408699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408571#post1408571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah being kin to Blackspirals by oath and Blood would be a major Redflag for anyone you would think!</div> </div> </div> </div>Question<br /> <br /> Were the Balor always tied to the Wyrm or did that only happen after the White Howlers were corrupted in Roman times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:03:54-07:00","id":1408705,"title":"","content":"They where always children of Balor and the Formirans which are pretty bad. But not knowingly serving the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:29:26-07:00","id":1408765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408699#post1408699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question<br /> <br /> Were the Balor always tied to the Wyrm or did that only happen after the White Howlers were corrupted in Roman times?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the blood ties with the tribe only happened after the fall of the Howlers. But the Wyrm seemed to have ties with primordial giants not just the Fomorians but also the Jotun, and the book Apocalypse has the giants aid the Wyrm in the Final Battle.<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s the fact that House Balor has unsavory practices and traditions and that naturally overlaps with creatures of darkness outside of Fae origin like Wyrm spirits. And We have the Paths of Balor which are the Trods most likely to lead to the Underworld or Wyrmish realms. The vault product about the Nightmare court seems to have the Fomorians be the origins of dark gods like the Neverborn and maybe the Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T16:20:14-07:00","id":1408805,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> one further question. Do you think House Balor only became Kin to the Cruithni (Pictish) peoples who were also Kinfolk to the White Howlers AFTER the Howlers fell to the Wyrm, or did this Kinship exist as far back as the War of Trees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T16:27:18-07:00","id":1408808,"title":"","content":"Their writeupin book of houses suggest the the latter. Through they didn\u2019t get alone well pre-Sprialimg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 08-17-2020, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T16:54:07-07:00","id":1408812,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T21:04:02-07:00","id":1408843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408805#post1408805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> one further question. Do you think House Balor only became Kin to the Cruithni (Pictish) peoples who were also Kinfolk to the White Howlers AFTER the Howlers fell to the Wyrm, or did this Kinship exist as far back as the War of Trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one thing to point out there are hints that the History the Changelings know of by the Time of Changeling the Dreaming was a fabrication, or a Dream History if you will, a lot of their history seems spurious, and this is especially pronounced in Dark Age Fae where they reveal there are no Kiths (though it could be interesting to do a Storyteller's vault product about a Zsplat of Kith) and there were only origins of Changeling, Firstborn and Inanimae (plus the elder dark of Charlies SV supplement). My headcanon to explain why everyone recalls things like evil Trolls since ancient times is that when the Fae underwent the Changeling Way Ritual en Masse they formed into Kiths based on Ideology and the Trolls chose Honor and Strength, perhaps even because some disliked their nature as bridge and cave dwelling monsters.<br /> <br /> So I believe House Balor didn't exist as a House as long as they believe they have. The White Howlers would have made Pacts with local Fae and some of those local fae would later form the House of Balor. In Between the forming of the Black Spiral Dancers and the Return of House Balor Both parties probably changed oodles since their predecessors probably made the first neighborly Truces during the Ice Age. And both being aligned towards self interest and the stewarding of unwholesome forces led to a stronger genuine alliance from what was likely more a truce of cooperation between Neighbors.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T04:53:05-07:00","id":1408884,"title":"","content":"Wow! I never thought of that, about the whole pre-Shattering history in Changeling being a fabrication. Probably because I never actually read Dark Ages Fae. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T05:59:10-07:00","id":1408897,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s like only one book for Dark Ages: Fae, so it\u2019s easy to miss it. Speaking of Dark Ages, I hope there\u2019s something else in the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:05:18-07:00","id":1408900,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is part of the Forming of Kiths is from pragmatism fae creatures banded together based off of agreed upon qualities of archetypes from the legends and beliefs of Mortals. So forming Kiths helped shield the fae from Banality using the Mortals own stories. And the Changeling Way Ritual was a potent Rite and if all Fae had to undergo it independently it would screw over the weakest and most numerous among them so by gathering into kiths they also shared a pool of viable bloodlines that acted as a vector of their reincarnation in future descendants. This way the strongest Fae led the Rite helping even the weakest rabble transition into half mortal changelings.<br /> <br /> I got into Dark Age Fae late too, so when I finally read it I was already informed about a lot of the neat lil connections and insinuations. One of the parts of the book even mentions how the alliance the Fianna have with the Fae is a prank that some fae used to help win a war with another group. I would have that be the general scuttlebutt but I would have it actually contain truth like those Fae outside of the British Isle's just assumed the Fianna were tricked, but those actually involved in the conflict were legitimate in consecrating Oaths of kinship.<br /> <br /> But if the setting of a game does assume the Changelings do have accurate recollection of history more or less, then House Balor would be a big no no for the Fianna, and the White Howlers probably made pacts with some nearby Unseelie, they also had connections with ghosts, but non of these allies were really making a difference when they decided to siege Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Its interesting to note in Shining Host they bring up that fae myth has it the Sidhe slew the Tuatha but people consider it impolite to talk about that possibility. But it makes sense on a few levels, like it might be that the Tuatha were just the True Fae opposed to the Fomorians rather then a special group of Super Fae, and through the changeling way most Fae became Changelings with some still left in the Dreaming. The other resonant note in that myth is it kind of aligns with mortal myths because essentially the Tuatha and even the Fomorians were succeeded by younger generations when their chieftains would die or retire, so they very much replaced by their kids and often their kids were the ones that slew them. After the Fae agreed to live under the hills that might have been the milestone where all new fae after that point wasn't considered Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:06:58-07:00","id":1408901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408897#post1408897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s like only one book for Dark Ages: Fae, so it\u2019s easy to miss it. Speaking of Dark Ages, I hope there\u2019s something else in the line?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> God I wish there was more to come. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We did get another taste of the Fae in the Darkening Sky Book, and the minichapter on the Elder Dark by Charlie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:28:42-07:00","id":1408909,"title":"","content":"I think the Fianna were allied with some of the Sidhe Houses, just not Balor.<br /> <br /> Also, I always assumed the Tuatha were the ancestors of the Sidhe. Am I wrong about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:54:44-07:00","id":1408914,"title":"","content":"What I didn\u2019t like is that the Menehune and Nunnihi can no longer gather glamour from Dreamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:54:44-07:00","id":1408915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408909#post1408909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Fianna were allied with some of the Sidhe Houses, just not Balor.<br /> <br /> Also, I always assumed the Tuatha were the ancestors of the Sidhe. Am I wrong about this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah the Fianna were especially allied to the Fiona House. Silverfangs were allied with Gwydion, so I guess Gwydion expanded into Mainland Europe.<br /> <br /> The definition of Tuatha was never fully explained. They may have been the God Progenitors of the Fae with the Sidhe as their inheritors. In Dark Age sense this would mean the Sidhe are beings known as Firstborn, so Fae born from the source, the Mists. The Commoners are mostly then from Changelings, the Dark Age Changelings were babies of the Fae raised by mortals or mortal babies raised by the Fae, and this means commoners being locked into Earth seems more fitting as they are halfway tied to it by their very nature.<br /> <br /> The other Option is that all the Olden Fae (or at least the Old Sidhe) where Tuatha or Fomorian, at least in Europe, and the modern Changelings don't necessarily know that.<br /> <br /> So its either the Changelings were literally the Tuatha but they don't realize it, or the Tuatha were especially powerful Godlike Fae and the Sidhe were their descendants with the commoners descended from their servants/bastards/converted Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Now the Fomorians could have just been one or two of the Season Courts, particularly Winter but maybe some aspects of Autumn. If we go with Charlie' the Fomorians are one step further then the Dark Fae, they are actually beings from the Darkness beyond the Mists that are even more antithetical to the world of men than the Court of Winter which is composed of monsters.<br /> <br /> Changeling leaves it a mystery because crossing the Mists in the Deep Dreaming strips the Fae Soul of divine truths when they return to the Autumn World.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T07:04:34-07:00","id":1408917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408914#post1408914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right