om the source, the Mists. The Commoners are mostly then from Changelings, the Dark Age Changelings were babies of the Fae raised by mortals or mortal babies raised by the Fae, and this means commoners being locked into Earth seems more fitting as they are halfway tied to it by their very nature.<br /> <br /> The other Option is that all the Olden Fae (or at least the Old Sidhe) where Tuatha or Fomorian, at least in Europe, and the modern Changelings don't necessarily know that.<br /> <br /> So its either the Changelings were literally the Tuatha but they don't realize it, or the Tuatha were especially powerful Godlike Fae and the Sidhe were their descendants with the commoners descended from their servants/bastards/converted Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Now the Fomorians could have just been one or two of the Season Courts, particularly Winter but maybe some aspects of Autumn. If we go with Charlie' the Fomorians are one step further then the Dark Fae, they are actually beings from the Darkness beyond the Mists that are even more antithetical to the world of men than the Court of Winter which is composed of monsters.<br /> <br /> Changeling leaves it a mystery because crossing the Mists in the Deep Dreaming strips the Fae Soul of divine truths when they return to the Autumn World.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that the Sidhe are descended from the Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T21:04:31-07:00","id":1409073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a