"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409074#post1409074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought everyone basically ignored that and allowed individual Nunnehi to choose which route to go...Nature or Dreamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll gut that and say the Nunnihi can do both, the Kithins could do both if they where in their native lands and not Colonial dreams,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:35:24-07:00","id":1409224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409130#post1409130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ll gut that and say the Nunnihi can do both, the Kithins could do both if they where in their native lands and not Colonial dreams,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems fair and good to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:31:16-07:00","id":1409348,"title":"","content":"By the way there\u2019s a weird thing with the Unseelie where the game says their not evil, but all the Unseelie are massive dicks, that do t follow the Unseelie code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T22:53:49-07:00","id":1409470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409348#post1409348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way there\u2019s a weird thing with the Unseelie where the game says their not evil, but all the Unseelie are massive dicks, that do t follow the Unseelie code.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's a dissonance that's been their since the 1E corebook. According to the whole gothic-punk aesthetic the unseelie are the wild and free rebels that we're meant to sympathize with, but instead a very large percentage of all the unseelie examples we're given throughout the entire run are kind of just assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T04:31:47-07:00","id":1409511,"title":"","content":"Yeah not to mention the poor \u201crebels\u201d against the Tyranny of the Seelie court, want to rule over Humans and according to the Enchanted own lots of slaves. So just like the American Revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:29:44-07:00","id":1409523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spook359</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409470#post1409470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's a dissonance that's been their since the 1E corebook. According to the whole gothic-punk aesthetic the unseelie are the wild and free rebels that we're meant to sympathize with, but instead a very large percentage of all the unseelie examples we're given throughout the entire run are kind of just assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> interesting analogy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:36:35-07:00","id":1409525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409511#post1409511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah not to mention the poor \u201crebels\u201d against the Tyranny of the Seelie court, want to rule over Humans and according to the Enchanted own lots of slaves. So just like the American Revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah the Dougal section of Book of Houses also seemed to correlate having Enchanted as having slaves. They mention some wanting to make it possible for enchanted gain membership in the House but those against the idea claim House Dougal doesn't use slaves. But it is interesting that the option for NonChangelings to gain Titles is on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:38:22-07:00","id":1409527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409130#post1409130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ll gut that and say the Nunnihi can do both, the Kithins could do both if they where in their native lands and not Colonial dreams,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you think like House Fiona in Hibernia could treat the Mounds as a natural source of glamour and Redcaps in the Kingdom of Alba could do the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T06:15:01-07:00","id":1409539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409527#post1409527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you think like House Fiona in Hibernia could treat the Mounds as a natural source of glamour and Redcaps in the Kingdom of Alba could do the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep exactly. The Fae in America don\u2019t know this after spending so much time away, and it\u2019s not like the European Fae would want random outsiders Raiding their Precious source of land Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T06:29:39-07:00","id":1409543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409539#post1409539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep exactly. The Fae in America don\u2019t know this after spending so much time away, and it\u2019s not like the European Fae would want random outsiders Raiding their Precious source of land Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do the Houses share these secrets among their members? Or are the motherland House members keeping quite? This really makes it strange that House Varich didn't become Tsars of the Motherlands but chose meager territories in America with their High Lord of the House just living in San Francisco.<br /> <br /> And how do you treat say Pooka? Do we go with the Brittish Isle because that is where the story came from or do we go with the Idea that Pooka are more a global Kith?<br /> <br /> It is an interesting option that all fae are actually tied to a specific homeland that they can gain succor from. And I do want literal Sidhe Courts held within the mounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T06:42:43-07:00","id":1409548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409543#post1409543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do the Houses share these secrets among their members? Or are the motherland House members keeping quite? This really makes it strange that House Varich didn't become Tsars of the Motherlands but chose meager territories in America with their High Lord of the House just living in San Francisco.<br /> <br /> And how do you treat say Pooka? Do we go with the Brittish Isle because that is where the story came from or do we go with the Idea that Pooka are more a global Kith?<br /> <br /> It is an interesting option that all fae are actually tied to a specific homeland that they can gain succor from. And I do want literal Sidhe Courts held within the mounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pooka are a odd one as animal tricksters seems to be pretty global, I\u2019ll rule it where their \u201ctotem\u201d species has a regular breeding population. But that means dog pooka could gain glamour from all over place, while the tiger pooka would need to go to India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:20:36-07:00","id":1409673,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think of the part in Kingdom of Willows where a group of Welsh fae colonize the American Southeast during the Dark Ages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:29:38-07:00","id":1409676,"title":"","content":"What, isn\u2019t that based on pseudoscience racist history that White people built south Eastern Structures, cause Indians where to dumb to. Plus why would the Nunnihi allow them to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.badarchaeology.com/controversies/a-medieval-welsh-colony-in-north-america/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.badarchaeology.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/09/madog_book.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.badarchaeology.com/controversies/a-medieval-welsh-colony-in-north-america/\" target=\"_blank\"> A medieval Welsh colony in America? - Bad Archaeology </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.badarchaeology.com/controversies/a-medieval-welsh-colony-in-north-america/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.badarchaeology.com/controversies/a-medieval-welsh-colony-in-north-america/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Prince Madoc and the European discovery of North America In 1580, Dr John Dee (1527-1608&times;9), the well known scientist, charlatan and consultant to Queen Elizabeth I, presented the Queen with a document, Title Royal, in which he claimed that &ldquo;the Lord Madoc, sonne of Owen Gwynedd, Prince of Northwales, led a Colonie and inhabited in [&hellip;] </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:33:35-07:00","id":1409678,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s based on a real (?) Welsh legend, the legend of Prince Madoc ap Gwynedd. And according to Kingdom of Willows the Nunnehi resisted violently and somewhat successfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T20:12:17-07:00","id":1409686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madoc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/01madog07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madoc\" target=\"_blank\"> Madoc - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madoc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madoc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its beyond dubious as RL history, but for Changeling who knows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:01:25-07:00","id":1409709,"title":"","content":"Thank you<br /> <br /> No, I definitely don\u2019t think it\u2019s real. (I know this didn\u2019t really happen, I just wasn\u2019t sure if this was a real legend or if novelist Madeleine L\u2019Engle made it up.) But in Kingdom of Willows Duke Meilge talks about being a member of a faerie expedition that settled the American Southeast during the Dark Ages. And the existence of Lord Tamlin, a Fiona Lost One with a freehold in Tennessee, depends on the idea that there were European fae in North America before the Shattering.<br /> <br /> Was this retconned by C20? Should it be retconned by C20?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I don\u2019t think it\u2019s racist, especially since Nunnehi pressures and the Shattering combine to basically wipe out the entire colony without a trace, but I could be wrong. Feel free to convince me either way if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-22-2020, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:07:28-07:00","id":1409712,"title":"","content":"Or you could make it that it was just Lord Tamlin and his Enchanted True Love Janet and their kids and maybe a couple retainers who settle in America before the Shattering and scrap the whole idea of a grand European fae expedition.<br /> <br /> Also, Kingdom of Willows never uses the name Madoc, but it does talk about European fae settling the American South before the Shattering. I just knew Madoc\u2019s name from non-gaming sources (the kids\u2019 novel A Swiftly Tilting Planet), so I kind of conflated the two ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-22-2020, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T14:24:43-07:00","id":1411120,"title":"","content":"Someone on a very old Changeling chat stated that the fae started as local things, then spread across the world. I'm fine with the &quot;this far and no farther&quot; nature of the oath struck by Tamlin and the local Nunnehi. Still have an entire mountain to tunnel through. And it's not like *every* meeting between Nunnehi and Kithain was hostile. I can see a sluagh being content to live in a hollowed out tree freehold, with the occasional visitor.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T21:26:06-07:00","id":1411164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1411120#post1411120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone on a very old Changeling chat stated that the fae started as local things, then spread across the world. I'm fine with the &amp;quot;this far and no farther&amp;quot; nature of the oath struck by Tamlin and the local Nunnehi. Still have an entire mountain to tunnel through. And it's not like *every* meeting between Nunnehi and Kithain was hostile. I can see a sluagh being content to live in a hollowed out tree freehold, with the occasional visitor.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T16:28:36-07:00","id":1418116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1408330#post1408330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the 90s, there was a website of fan material for the various World of Darkness gamelines called B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness. One guy made a bunch of Kith submissions based on real-world beliefs about inhuman but humanoid creatures from around the world. At one point, for ease of reference, I copied all of them onto an Angelfire-hosted website. B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness has long since disappeared from the web; but the copy I made is still out there. Indeed, I couldn't take it down even if I wanted to: I've long since lost both the email address and the password that I used to set up that archive. <br /> <br /> Note that this predated the Hsien. But my own head-canon has always held that Changeling's have always had a much more diverse selection of Kiths throughout the world, including in East Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you track down a copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T04:26:57-07:00","id":1418172,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/ca4/dataweaver/play/changeling\" target=\"_blank\">The Changeling Archive</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T11:02:09-07:00","id":1418217,"title":"","content":"Thank you,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T17:16:51-07:00","id":1418270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1409709#post1409709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you<br /> <br /> No, I definitely don\u2019t think it\u2019s real. (I know this didn\u2019t really happen, I just wasn\u2019t sure if this was a real legend or if novelist Madeleine L\u2019Engle made it up.) But in Kingdom of Willows Duke Meilge talks about being a member of a faerie expedition that settled the American Southeast during the Dark Ages. And the existence of Lord Tamlin, a Fiona Lost One with a freehold in Tennessee, depends on the idea that there were European fae in North America before the Shattering.<br /> <br /> Was this retconned by C20? Should it be retconned by C20?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I don\u2019t think it\u2019s racist, especially since Nunnehi pressures and the Shattering combine to basically wipe out the entire colony without a trace, but I could be wrong. Feel free to convince me either way if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just think it\u2019s uneessrcy as a excuse for the Sidhe to claim American freeholds, just have them say that this secret oath, from the early Middle Ages that says the Sidhe have the right to any newly discovered freehold, and if not , they have no right to complain about the Sidhe taking them back, after all they stole it from the Nunnihi, also the idea of white settlers pre-Colombian has a very racist origin . <a href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/white-settlers-buried-truth-about-midwests-mysterious-mound-cities-180968246/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/histo...ies-180968246/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T19:08:19-07:00","id":1418282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1377908-what-do-you-think-of-the-metaplot-advances-in-c20?p=1418270#post1418270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I just think it\u2019s uneessrcy as a excuse for the Sidhe to claim American freeholds, just have them say that this secret oath, from the early Middle Ages that says the Sidhe have the right to any newly discovered freehold, and if not , they have no right to complain about the Sidhe taking them back, after all they stole it from the Nunnihi, also the idea of white settlers pre-Colombian has a very racist origin . <a href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/white-settlers-buried-truth-about-midwests-mysterious-mound-cities-180968246/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/histo...ies-180968246/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I read the article you linked. Wow. I see your point. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}